<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    Verified against the upstream repository on 2026-10-16.

    This file used to advertise three builds: 25.7.22 as stable and 25.8.14 as alpha.
    Neither tag exists upstream, and both download URLs return HTTP 404, so every visitor
    was sent to a dead link.

    What actually resolves:
      - GET /releases lists only 24.10.16-beta and 24.10.27, both prereleases.
      - 25.7.23 exists and is reachable by tag, with prerelease=false, but is not in that
        listing. Its assets are VDD.Control.25.7.23.zip, VirtualDisplayDriver-x86.Driver.Only.zip,
        VirtualDisplayDriver-ARM64.Driver.Only.zip and VirtualAudioDriver-x86.Driver.Only.zip.

    So there is exactly one resolvable Virtual Driver Control build, and it is listed here
    under <release>. Calling it stable is a judgement this file cannot make on the
    maintainer's behalf: upstream marks no non-prerelease release. If a channel marker is
    wanted back, restore <beta>/<alpha> and give each a build that exists.
-->
<versions>
    <release>
        <name>Virtual Driver Control</name>
        <build>25.7.23</build>
        <link>https://github.com/VirtualDrivers/Virtual-Display-Driver/releases/download/25.7.23/VDD.Control.25.7.23.zip</link>
        <description>The only Virtual Driver Control build upstream currently resolves. Portable, no installer, supports Install/Uninstall and RELOAD_DRIVER over the driver pipe. Upstream marks no non-prerelease release, so treat "stable" here as "newest that exists", not as a maintainer designation.</description>
    </release>
</versions>